{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Double_Energy","to":"Double Energy"},{"from":"Secret_Weapon","to":"Secret Weapon"},{"from":"Wreath_of_Flame","to":"Wreath of Flame"},{"from":"Crush_Joints","to":"Crush Joints"},{"from":"Deva_Form","to":"Deva Form"},{"from":"Hand_of_Greed","to":"Hand of Greed"},{"from":"Storm_of_Steel","to":"Storm of Steel"},{"from":"Good_Instincts","to":"Good Instincts"},{"from":"White_Noise","to":"White Noise"},{"from":"Spot_Weakness","to":"Spot Weakness"},{"from":"Well-Laid_Plans","to":"Well-Laid Plans"}],"pages":{"1794":{"pageid":1794,"ns":0,"title":"Acrobatics","revisions":[{"revid":56192,"parentid":55259,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Acrobatics\n| Image       = Green-Acrobatics.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Draw (3;4) cards.<br>Discard 1 card.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw, Discard\n}}\n{{C|Acrobatics}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 3 (4 if upgraded) cards and makes you select 1 card in hand to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]].\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Order ===\n* Selecting a card to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] happens ''after'' drawing, meaning that you can also choose one of the newly drawn cards to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]].\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Acrobatics}}'s [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics: \n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' this turn.\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy.\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Acrobatics}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2313":{"pageid":2313,"ns":0,"title":"Apotheosis","revisions":[{"revid":56321,"parentid":50739,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Apotheosis\n| Image       = Colorless-Apotheosis.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| CostPlus    = 1\n| Description = {{KW|Upgrade}} ALL your cards for the rest of combat.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Upgrade\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Upgrade}}{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Apotheosis}} is a 2 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It {{KW|Upgrade|upgrades}} every card in the player's hand, draw pile, discard pile, and exhaust pile.\n\n== Obtaining Apotheosis ==\n{{C|Apotheosis}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n\n* Cards that are created ''after'' {{C|Apotheosis}} has already been played (such as the {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} created by {{C|Blade Dance}}, the random cards created by {{R|Dead Branch}}, or cards generated by {{P|Attack Potion}}, {{P|Skill Potion}}, or {{P|Power Potion}}) will not be {{KW|Upgrade|upgraded}}.\n* Since {{C|Apotheosis}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}, playing it while having {{R|Dead Branch}} will add a random card to the player's hand. However, {{C|Apotheosis}} will trigger its effect before {{R|Dead Branch}} creates the card, so it will not be {{KW|Upgrade|upgraded}}.\n* {{C|Apotheosis}} does not {{KW|Upgrade|upgrade}} itself.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n\n* Using {{R|Bottled Lightning}} to put {{C|Apotheosis}} in the player's starting hand can allow them to immediately {{KW|Upgrade|upgrade}} all their cards at the start of combat.\n* {{C|Master Reality}} can be used to {{KW|Upgrade|upgrade}} cards that are created after {{C|Apotheosis}} is played, since its effect only {{KW|Upgrade|upgrades}} the cards that the player currently has in their hand, draw pile, discard pile, and exhaust pile.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n\n* {{C|Armaments}} may only be able to {{KW|Upgrade|upgrade}} cards before {{C|Apotheosis}} is played.\n** If the player has cards or other effects that generate cards in the middle of combat, then {{C|Armaments}} will be able to {{KW|Upgrade|upgrade}} them as normal since they will not have been {{KW|Upgrade|upgraded}} by {{C|Apotheosis}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n\n* \"Apotheosis\" is the act of becoming divine or god-like<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apotheosis</ref>.\n* The card art for Apotheosis is reminiscent of the art for the Priest talent of the same name in Blizzard Entertainment's ''World of Warcraft''<ref>https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Apotheosis</ref> and may have been the inspiration for its art in Slay the Spire.\n** The same art from World of Warcraft was re-used for the Hearthstone card of the same name<ref>https://hearthstone.wiki.gg/wiki/Apotheosis</ref>, also developed by Blizzard Entertainment and set in the Warcraft universe.\n\n== Update History ==\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** The word \"all\" is all-caps in certain scenarios. These scenarios are: When it refers to all enemies and when referring to cards that are outside of your hand (Apotheosis).\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Apotheosis now costs {{Icon|CE}}2. Upgrades to cost {{Icon|CE}}1. (Previously cost {{Icon|CE}}0, with the upgrade making it {{KW|Innate}}).\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2028":{"pageid":2028,"ns":0,"title":"Caltrops","revisions":[{"revid":55680,"parentid":50497,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Caltrops\n|Image       = Green-Caltrops.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Whenever you are attacked, deal (3;5) damage back.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Thorns}}\n{{C|Caltrops}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 3 (5 if upgraded) {{BD|Thorns}}, which deals that amount of damage to every enemy that hits you.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Only activates upon being hit by an enemy attack, so not when taking damage from:\n** {{BD|Sharp Hide}} or {{BD|Thorns}}.\n** {{BD|Explosive}}\n** {{BD|Constricted}}\n** {{BD|Beat of Death}}\n** Any damage from one of your cards, such as {{C|Burn}}, {{C|Pain}} or {{C|Bloodletting}}.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1912":{"pageid":1912,"ns":0,"title":"Carnage","revisions":[{"revid":56738,"parentid":50414,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Carnage\n| Image       = Red-Carnage.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = {{KW|Ethereal}}.<br>Deal (20;28) damage.\n| GivesToPlayer = Ethereal\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Ethereal}}\n{{C|Carnage}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 20 (30 if upgraded) damage. It has {{KW|Ethereal}}, which means it will {{KW|Exhaust}} if it is in your hand when you end your turn.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Carnage card buff: 18 -> 20. Upgraded: 26 -> 28\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** We removed one level of unlocks! Three additional cards are now available by default in the card pool for both The Silent and Ironclad. The following cards are now added to the card pool by default: Ghostly Armor, Carnage, Entrench\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2103":{"pageid":2103,"ns":0,"title":"Chill","revisions":[{"revid":56935,"parentid":55691,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Chill\n|Image       = Blue-Chill.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. <br>){{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}} for each enemy in combat.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Innate, Channel, Frost, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}} {{Keyword Infobox|Frost}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Chill}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}. It {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 1 {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} for each enemy currently in combat, then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. When upgraded, it becomes {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always appear in your first hand of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Chill only counts enemies currently in combat at the time it is played.  If an enemy dies because of an orb that was {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} because of {{C|Chill}}, the number of Orbs Channeled by it will not be affected.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* As Chill+ is {{KW|Innate}}, it works well with:\n** {{R|Bag of Preparation}}, allowing you to draw plenty of non-Innate cards as well.\n** {{R|Gambling Chip}}, allowing you to discard it away if not needed on the first turn.\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Chill works best with other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, allowing Orbs to be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} more frequently. <!--- No idea what to include as prototypical orb gen cards, so just went with these two--->\n* {{C|Blizzard}} does more damage for each {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making Orbs generated by Chill less effective.\n* Many fights do not do much damage on the first turn, so having other sources of first turn {{KW|Block}}, such as {{R|Anchor}} or {{C|Boot Sequence}}, may make upgrading Chill unnecessary, and sometimes even inadvisable.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* There are two fights where Chill may {{KW|Channel}} as many as 5 Orbs, [[Reptomancer]] and the [[Slimes#Acid Slime (S)|Slime Gang]] hallway fight. As such, it is second only to {{C|Tempest}} in terms of potential Orb output for a single card.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2283":{"pageid":2283,"ns":0,"title":"Crush Joints","revisions":[{"revid":56952,"parentid":55714,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Crush Joints\n|Image       = Purple-CrushJoints.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (8;10) damage.<br>If the last card played this combat was a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}, apply (1;2) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Vulnerable\n}}\n{{C|Crush Joints}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 8 (10 if upgraded) damage. If the last card played this combat was a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}, this card also applies 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Crush Joints' [[Beta Art]] shows the {{M|Transient}}, an [[Act 3]] enemy which loses {{BD|Strength}} equal to the amount of damage it takes each turn. \n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2325":{"pageid":2325,"ns":0,"title":"Deva Form","revisions":[{"revid":55738,"parentid":50698,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Deva Form\n|Image       = Purple-DevaForm.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|Description = ({{KW|Ethereal}}.<br>;)At the start of your turn, gain {{Icon|PE}} <br>and increase this gain by 1.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Deva}}{{Keyword Infobox|Ethereal}}\n{{C|Deva Form}} is a 3 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It will give one {{BD|Deva}}. Unless upgraded, '''Deva Form''' has {{KW|Ethereal}}, which means it will {{KW|Exhaust}} if it is in your hand when you end your turn.\n\n{{BD|Deva}} grants the player gains additional {{KW|Energy}} at the beginning of each turn, starting at 1 {{KW|Energy}} and increasing by 1 every subsequent turn. For example, if the player normally gains 3 {{KW|Energy}} every turn and '''Deva Form''' is played on the 2nd turn, the player will have 4 {{KW|Energy}} on the 3rd turn and 5 {{KW|Energy}} on the 4th turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Deva Form}} synergizes well with {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''-hungry cards, such as X-cost cards and cards with high {{Icon|PE}}-cost.\n* {{BD|Deva}} quickly trivializes the downside of {{C|Fasting}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* A deva is a Hindu term for a deity. Though the Watcher is female, deva is a masculine term; the feminine equivalent is devi.\n* The card art depicts the relics {{R|Singing Bowl}}, {{R|Vajra}}, and {{R|Juzu Bracelet}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2130":{"pageid":2130,"ns":0,"title":"Double Energy","revisions":[{"revid":53380,"parentid":50586,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Double Energy\n|Image       = Blue-DoubleEnergy.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Double your {{KW|Energy}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{C|Double Energy}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. <!-- It doubles your current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''. -->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost of an unupgraded {{C|Double Energy}} is payed before the card takes effect. For example, if you have 3 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' and play an unupgraded {{C|Double Energy}}, you will go to 2 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''', which will then be doubled, leaving you with 4 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* It synergizes well with other ways to build up {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''', such as {{C|TURBO}} or any relics that give additional {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n* {{R|Ice Cream}} can both be used to increase the effectiveness of {{C|Double Energy}}, as well as maintain excess {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' generated by it for future use.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2448":{"pageid":2448,"ns":0,"title":"Forethought","revisions":[{"revid":50727,"parentid":42767,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Forethought\n|Image       = Colorless-Forethought.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Put (a card;any number of cards) from your hand to the bottom of your draw pile. (It costs;They cost) 0 until played.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Forethought}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to pick one card (or any number of cards if upgraded) from your hand and put it on the bottom of your draw pile. The picked card(s) will cost 0 '''Energy''' until played.\n\n== Obtaining Forethought ==\n{{C|Forethought}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||Obtain an}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon&color:Colorless|Uncommon Colorless}} {{TS|green||Card}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* In the case of an upgraded {{C|Forethought}}, the order in which the cards are picked will determine the order in which they are placed at the bottom of your draw pile, meaning the card that was picked first will be the first card that is drawn, and the card that was picked will be the last card that is drawn.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The discount originating from this card will also be copied when the affected card is copied by {{C|Nightmare}} or {{C|Dual Wield}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Normality card not stopping cards affected by Setup and Forethought.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Fix for Mummified Hand relic targeting cards with costs lowered by Setup or Forethought.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Forethought card wording improvements.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Card copy effects like Dual Wield should now also copy the \"free to play once\" effect from cards like Setup and Forethought.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Forethought.\n** Wrist Blade relic now works with cards that are cost 0 via Setup or Forethought.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2446":{"pageid":2446,"ns":0,"title":"Good Instincts","revisions":[{"revid":50728,"parentid":36929,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Good Instincts\n|Image       = Colorless-GoodInstincts.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Gain (6;9) {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Good Instincts}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 6 (9 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Obtaining Good Instincts ==\n{{C|Good Instincts}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Good Instincts card buffed. Block increased from 5 -> 6.\n** Good Instincts+ card buffed. Block increased from 8 -> 9.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Good Instincts card buff: 4 -> 5 Block. Good Instincts+: 7 -> 8 Block.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Good instincts+. 4 -> 7 Block.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1873":{"pageid":1873,"ns":0,"title":"Hand of Greed","revisions":[{"revid":56412,"parentid":56125,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Hand of Greed\n| Image       = Colorless-HandofGreed.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal (20;25) damage.<br>If {{KW|Fatal}}, gain (20;25) Gold.\n| InteractsWith = Fatal\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Fatal}}\n{{C|Hand of Greed}} is a 2 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 20 (25 if upgraded) damage, and if this damage is {{KW|Fatal}}, it will give 20 (25 if upgraded) [[Gold]].\n\n== Obtaining Hand of Greed ==\n{{C|Hand of Greed}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} Card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As playing {{C|Hand of Greed}} at the right moment is crucial, it synergizes with {{R|Runic Pyramid}} and ways to {{KW|Retain}} it, such as {{C|Well-Laid Plans}}, {{C|Equilibrium}} or {{C|Meditate}}.\n\n* {{R|Bloody Idol}} will heal you for 5 HP when gaining [[Gold]] through this card\n** As this gives healing in combat, it be boosted by {{R|Magic Flower}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Despite being a card that has effects that remain outside of combat, {{C|Hand of Greed}} can be generated within combat through effects like {{C|Magnetism}}, {{P|Colorless Potion}}, {{R|Toolbox}} and {{C|Foreign Influence}}.\n\n* When duplicated through an effect such as {{C|Double Tap}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}, {{C|Lesson Learned}} will trigger its {{KW|Fatal}} effect even if only the second play was {{KW|Fatal}}.\n** As duplicated {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} always target the same enemy with both plays, you cannot trigger {{C|Lesson Learned}} twice by duplicating it.  \n<!-- omniscience is weird about this, but I don't exactly remember right now in what way -->\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} does ''not'' trigger when {{BD|Minion|Minions}} are killed.\n** However, the {{M|Cultist}} enemies in {{M|Awakened One}} fight are not technically {{BD|Minion|Minions}}, and ''can'' trigger {{KW|Fatal}}.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} is not affected by {{M|Slime Boss}} or other Slime enemies splitting, and only triggers when reducing a Slime's health to 0, whether that Slime was spawned as the result of a split or not.\n* The first phase of {{M|Awakened One}} does not trigger {{KW|Fatal}}, but the second phase does.\n\n* In the {{M|Darkling|Three Darklings}} fight, an attack is only considered {{KW|Fatal}} if it kills the last {{M|Darkling}}; otherwise, unlimited triggers could be farmed on this fight.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} triggers on killing the {{M|Corrupt Heart}}, although this does not matter, as it ends the run.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Due to the limited number of {{KW|Fatal}} triggers available in any given combat, {{C|Hand of Greed}} does not synergize with other {{KW|Fatal}} cards:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Ritual Dagger}}\n* {{C|Feed}}\n* {{C|Lesson Learned}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fatal keyword added for cards which have effects upon killing a non-Minion enemy.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Title capitalization for Hand Of Greed -> Hand of Greed.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Hand Of Greed card buff: 15 -> 20 damage. Hand of Greed+: 20 -> 25 damage.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Hand of Greed card now gives gold instantly, rather than through VFX (triggered Bloody Idol).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Hand of Greed.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2311":{"pageid":2311,"ns":0,"title":"Perseverance","revisions":[{"revid":54862,"parentid":50673,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Perseverance\n|Image       = Purple-Perseverance.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}.<br>Gain (5;7) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Whenever this card is {{KW|Retain|Retained}}, increase its {{KW|Block}} by (2;3).\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}} {{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Perseverance}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 (7 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn, and it will increase the {{KW|Block}} gained by 2 (3 if upgraded) whenever it is {{KW|Retain|Retained}} at the end of your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As it {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2466":{"pageid":2466,"ns":0,"title":"Secret Weapon","revisions":[{"revid":50749,"parentid":36949,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Secret Weapon\n|Image       = Colorless-SecretWeapon.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Put an Attack from your draw pile into your hand.(<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.;)\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Secret Weapon}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to select an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card from your draw pile and place it in your hand. If this {{C|Secret Weapon}} is not upgraded, it {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Obtaining Secret Weapon ==\n{{C|Secret Weapon}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Secret Technique+ and Secret Weapon+. Removes Exhaust on upgrade.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Wording for select screens for Secret Tech and Secret Attack cards improved.\n** Secret Tech and Secret Attack when bursted with full hand no longer breaks the Hand.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2259":{"pageid":2259,"ns":0,"title":"Skim","revisions":[{"revid":50606,"parentid":36258,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Skim\n|Image       = Blue-Skim.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Draw (3;4) cards.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Skim}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 3 (4 if upgraded) cards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1528":{"pageid":1528,"ns":0,"title":"Spot Weakness","revisions":[{"revid":56354,"parentid":55955,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Spot Weakness\n| Image       = Red-SpotWeakness.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = If the enemy intends to attack, gain (3;4) {{BD|Strength}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Strength\n}} \n{{Power Infobox|Strength}}\n{{C|Spot Weakness}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}} if the target's [[Intent]] is to attack.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* When [[Intent|Intents]] are obscured by {{R|Runic Dome}}, it can be harder to know if this card will have an effect. However, {{C|Spot Weakness}} can still be played on a target, and this can be used to determine if the target is attacking when you are unsure.\n\n* It does not matter if the target's attack has an additional effect or deals 0 damage, as long as attacking is part of the [[Intent]], this card will activate its effects.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Spot Weakness rare crash fix.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1813":{"pageid":1813,"ns":0,"title":"Storm of Steel","revisions":[{"revid":56372,"parentid":55960,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Storm of Steel\n| Image       = Green-StormofSteel.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Discard your hand.<br>Add 1 {{C|Shiv}}(;+) into your hand for each card discarded.\n| GivesToPlayer = Discard\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Shiv}}{{C|Storm of Steel}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It [[Keywords#Discard|discards]] all cards in your hand, and then creates a {{C|Shiv}} ({{C|Shiv|Shiv+}} if upgraded) for every card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this way.\n\n== Interactions ==\n* The damage of each {{C|Shiv}} will be increased by the amount of {{BD|Accuracy}} you have, which can be obtained from {{C|Accuracy}}.\n\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of every {{C|Shiv}} by 4.\n\n* Anything that benefits from {{KW|Exhaust}} will be triggered by playing {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}.\n\n* {{R|Unceasing Top}} allows you to draw more cards after playing all {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} created by this card.\n\n* {{C|Storm of Steel}}'s [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics. However, as {{C|Storm of Steel}} practically replaces your hand with {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}, many of these cards will only be able to be played if they are somehow drawn after playing {{C|Storm of Steel}}, for example through [[Keywords#Discard|discarding]] {{C|Reflex}}, {{R|Ink Bottle}} or the aformentioned {{R|Unceasing Top}}.\n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects. However, as {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} cost 0, this {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' will likely be wasted unless more cards can be drawn after playing {{C|Storm of Steel}}.\n** {{R|Ice Cream}} ensures that the {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gained by {{C|Tactician}} can be useful, even if no more cards get drawn.\n\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by X {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' this turn, where X is the number of cards [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}} per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n** {{R|Ice Cream}} ensures that the {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gained by {{R|Hovering Kite}} can be useful, even if no more cards get drawn.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1838":{"pageid":1838,"ns":0,"title":"Warcry","revisions":[{"revid":56389,"parentid":50407,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Warcry\n| Image       = Red-Warcry.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Draw (1;2) (card;cards).<br>Put a card from your hand onto the top of your draw pile.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Warcry}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 1 card (2 cards if upgraded) and allows you to select one card in hand to place on top of your drawpile. {{C|Warcry}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Selecting the card to put on top of your draw pile happens ''after'' drawing, meaning a card drawn this way can potentially be placed right back on top.\n\n* Although {{C|Mayhem}} plays the top card of the draw pile, it cannot be used in tandem with {{C|Warcry}} to play a specific card, as {{C|Mayhem}} activates ''after'' cards are drawn at the start of your turn, meaning the card will already be in hand.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Warcry tweaked so the unupgraded form is buffed (cost 0, draw 1 place 1).\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2044":{"pageid":2044,"ns":0,"title":"Well-Laid Plans","revisions":[{"revid":56001,"parentid":55604,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Well-Laid Plans\n|Image       = Green-Well-LaidPlans.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = At the end of your turn, {{KW|Retain}} up to (1;2) (card;cards).\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Retain Cards}}{{C|Well-Laid Plans}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Although {{KW|Ethereal}} cards can be chosen to be retained using this card, they will still {{KW|Exhaust}} at the end of the turn.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Well-Laid Plans}}'s {{KW|Retain}} effect is redundant with {{R|Runic Pyramid}}.\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Well-Laid Plans card cost increased from 0 -> 1.\n\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Well-Laid Plans card plays slightly faster now.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Bird-Faced, Well-Laid, All-Out, Self-Forming gets hyphenated.\n** Dazed and Clumsy now exhaust even if retained via Well Laid Plans (all Ethereal cards).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Updated wording of Well Laid Plans to be simpler.\n** Always show confirmation button for Well Laid Plans even if you have \"Disable confirm 1 card\" on.\n** Don't prompt for Well Laid Plans if you have Runic Pyramid.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Reworked Well Laid Plans card.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2208":{"pageid":2208,"ns":0,"title":"White Noise","revisions":[{"revid":50612,"parentid":36263,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = White Noise\n|Image       = Blue-WhiteNoise.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Add a random Power card into your hand.<br>It costs 0 this turn.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|White Noise}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It will generate a random {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card, which will have its normal cost replaced by 0 for this turn. {{C|White Noise}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat such as cards that provide healing like {{C|Self Repair}}\n* Is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n\n== Notes ==\n{{C|White Noise}} can only generate cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like  Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2308":{"pageid":2308,"ns":0,"title":"Wreath of Flame","revisions":[{"revid":56006,"parentid":55608,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Wreath of Flame\n|Image       = Purple-WreathofFlame.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Your next Attack deals (5;8) additional damage.\n|Keywords    = Vigor\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vigor}}\n{{C|Wreath of Flame}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 (8 if upgraded) {{BD|Vigor}}, which increases the damage of every hit of the next {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card you play.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* The more often the next {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} hits, the more effective this card is. The {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} that most notably synergize with this card in this way are:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Flying Sleeves}}, {{C|Tantrum}} and {{C|Ragnarok}} can benefit from this multiple times, respectively 2, 3 or 4 if upgraded, and 5 or 6 if upgraded.\n* {{C|Bowling Bash}} and {{C|Expunger}} from {{C|Conjure Blade}} can hit a variable amount of times.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}